  Arrrgggh.  I lost my best hack game ever.  And not to any bugs or any
deficiency in hack whatsoever.  I had been cruising the dungeon in a game
that had been playing for about 10 minutes a day for the last 3-4 months.
I had identified some 400 pieces of armour, labouriously carrying every
piece of armour from level 1-30 onto a temple on level 10.  Rust monsters had
been genocided a while back.  No problems.

  Thus when I made the jump to level 50 to begin the great flight up, I had
armour class -22 and a +5 (was +8) Stormbringer.  In other words I was
cruising.  I found the Wizard on level 48, but decided to let him sleep
until I had found the other 18 staircases up.  (I had carefully cut
passageways and left food on each level to make for a speedy flight up.)
I had 30 real gems and 50,000 gp waiting for me on level one.  Then, on
level 44 I meet a Lich.  One of several, this creature dared to
disintegrate my speed boots!  I killed him for discourtesy, but I was down a 
vital piece of armour.  Oh well.

  Then on level 42, I was trading blow for blow with Asmodeus and his
henchman.  By the time Asmo went down, I was down to 75 of 210 hit points.
I teleport over to the Minotaur and start pounding him.  He starts pounding
back and when I was down to 40 hps, I decide to fight another day.  (I'm pretty
free and easy, I've got my amulet of life saving on.)  Sure enough, I teleport
away and I'm beside a cockatrice.  No problem, I have lizards galour and
I'm in good with my god.  Than suddenly, an evil grin crosses my face.
I've got *two* more of those blasted Liches to deal with on this level.
Let's see how they stand up to maniacs wielding cockatrices. 

  I wipe out the cockatrice with two blows and sure enough, it leaves a body.  I
pick it up with my +4 padded gloves, and t.p. over to the Minotaur.  It turns to
see me as I hit it with a meaty smack.  It laughs about adventurers hitting it
with dead chickens and stops when it notices it's turning to stone.  Last laugh
for the adventurer.  Now to show those Liches who's boss...

  One teleport and I'm beside the Lich.  
  
  "Bye bye lich", says I as I wind up the swing. 

  "Bye bye gloves", it croaks, and disintegrates the gloves.

  "Bye bye life", says the adventurer as he notices what he's holding and
obligingly turns to stone.

  BUT WAIT!!  There's an amulet of life saving!!  And miraculously the 
adventurer turns back from stone to flesh.

  The Lich grins and says "Get on with it.  I have better ways to waste my 
time." as he watches the intrepid adventurer continue to clutch his bird.
"A bird in the hand is worth a place in the high score list".  And indeed,
that's just what this adventurer got as he proceeded to instantly turn to
stone again without a move to rescue himself.

  Next time, the genocide nails liches.  I don't care if I'm on level 1, next
time, the liches bite the dust.

						Tom West


